{"file":"Tenet-2.2.7-v1.zip","bytes":168725,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"tenet","description":"A commitment ledger for decisions and rules. Records what you chose, why, and the condition that would reverse it — then comes back when that condition fires. Every rule carries what catches it when it breaks, or `none` and the reason; a rule with no answer is itself the defect.","version":"2.2.7","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/Hirannad/tenet","homepage":"https://github.com/Hirannad/tenet","keywords":["decisions","architecture-decision-record","adr","claude-md","instructions","knowledge","pkm","obsidian","claude-code"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/tenet-audit/SKILL.md","name":"tenet-audit","description":"Use when auditing, reviewing, iterating on, or improving CLAUDE.md and related instruction files (CLAUDE.local.md, .claude/rules/, AGENTS.md, managed policy) across global and project layers. Use when the user mentions CLAUDE.md audit, instruction-layer review, memory-file cleanup, checking Claude config against best practices, or whether the tool surface (permissions, plugins, skills, MCP servers) has grown.","headings":["CLAUDE.md Auditor","When to use","Workflow","1. Discover","2. Score","3. Cross-layer check","4. Report","5. Fix on approval","Quick rubric (one-line checklist)"],"name_hint":"tenet · 审查"},{"path":"skills/tenet-capture/SKILL.md","name":"tenet-capture","description":"Capture this session's decisions into the decision ledger, and review drafts waiting in the inbox. Distils what was decided, which options were weighed, what the dilemma was, and what would reverse the choice. Writes drafts only; a separate mechanical step promotes them once you have given a verdict.","headings":["Capture into the decision ledger","Mode 1 — distil this session","Mode 2 — review pending drafts","Hard rules"],"name_hint":"tenet · capture"},{"path":"skills/tenet-sweep/SKILL.md","name":"tenet-sweep","description":"Weekly housekeeping for the decision ledger. Sweeps for decisions whose reversal condition may now be met, plus dead links, orphans, stale drafts, unjustified raw files and an over-grown universal layer, then writes a short digest and proposes fixes without applying them. Use when the user asks for the weekly sweep or vault maintenance, wants to look through or tidy up their own decision notes, asks which recorded conditions may have fired since the last pass, or when a session-start notice says maintenance is overdue. It reviews the notes as a set; it does not search them for a fact.","headings":["Ledger maintenance","The checks","The digest","What this must never do"],"name_hint":"tenet · sweep"},{"path":"skills/tenet/SKILL.md","name":"tenet","description":"Consult the decision ledger — a personal journal of architectural, structural and methodological decisions, the reasoning behind them, and the conditions that would reverse them. Use before making or revisiting a design, architecture, tooling or process decision; when the user asks what was decided before, why something is the way it is, or whether a similar problem has already been reasoned through; and when a past decision may need reconsidering. Only surfaces what is in scope for the current directory.","headings":["The decision ledger","What is in scope right now","How scope works","Answering","When the user is about to decide something","References","Related skills"],"name_hint":"tenet"}],"commands":[],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["tenet","Always in scope — methodology, architecture, structure","The problem","What it does","What this is not","Compared to","Install","Getting started","With and without Obsidian","What the platform already does","Privacy","What it reads from Claude's own memory, exactly","Known limits"]},{"path":"vault-template/README.md","headings":["The vault","Layout","Note types","Admission rule for raw material","The three notes already here","Language","Where the rules live"]}],"m